-- CMS content backup — taken before the MIS landing-page CMS was removed.
--
-- The CMS let MIS admins override landing/nav/footer strings and serve markdown
-- pages. It was removed because nothing depended on it: the three `content.*`
-- permissions had zero role grants and all six cms_pages were unpublished and
-- empty. Landing copy now lives only in src/content/site.ts.
--
-- This file exists so nothing is unrecoverable. It holds every row from
-- cms_texts, cms_nav_items and cms_pages in both environments at the time of
-- removal, as of 2026-08-19.
--
-- To restore: first recreate the tables with the DDL in
--   prisma/migrations/20260730120000_cms_content/migration.sql
-- (kept in git history), then run the INSERT block for the environment you want.
--
-- Of note: 10 strings below were edited via the MIS UI and never made it back
-- into src/content/site.ts, so prod was rendering them instead of the code
-- values. They were intentionally NOT ported during removal — the code copy was
-- chosen as the source of truth. Paths, if you ever want them back:
--   landing hero.title / hero.emphasizedTitle / hero.description /
--           hero.genieImageAlt / hero.wishCards.1.title /
--           journeys.candidateLabel / journeys.employer.0.title /
--           highlights.2.points.0
--   footer  legalLine / statusLabel

